{
 "slice": "campaign-close-charge-price",
 "status": "landed",
 "decisions": [
  "D-11",
  "D-97",
  "R-15/R-18 clause 2"
 ],
 "what_this_slice_is": "The R-15/R-18 amendment's clause 2, fired. standing-dissent-docket.json's syndra_cast_timeline_ordinal row records that its clause 1 re-adjudication ran, was well posed, and certified NEITHER committed side of fights/manual_target/cast_timeline[1]/resource_cost in either scenario; the re-adjudication that followed sustained the dissent on the value the whole-series computation states. Clause 2 re-opens the producing correction as a ruled src/ slice rather than absorbing the address into a baseline, and this is that slice: C6's recast_of=\"Q\" stamp gave the scheduler a second Dark Sphere charge to place and the engine priced that charge at nothing. It now pays Dark Sphere's own mana.",
 "the_correction": {
  "was": "Syndra's Q2 row carried no resource_cost at all. champions/engine.py's _stamp_resource_cost reaches a cost row only through the slot's OWN ability JSON, and a synthetic slot has none (ctx.ability() is None for Q2), so the stamp returned early and every consumer read the absent key through its own get(..., 0.0) default. A stocked charge was free.",
  "now": "The module prices its own synthetic slot: resource_type off Q's cached resource field and resource_cost off Q's own cost row at Q's rank, through the new slotlib.extract_resource_cost. The engine's free-recast branch is unchanged and still applies to a recast that one paid cast bought (Camille's and Ambessa's Q2); that is not what a charge is.",
  "the_source_that_decides_it": "data/champions.json, Syndra Q, effect 2: \"Transcendent Bonus: Collecting 40 Splinters of Wrath causes Syndra to periodically stock a Dark Sphere charge, up to a maximum of 2.\" The charge gates availability and says nothing about price; Q's own cost row is [40, 45, 50, 55, 60] with resource MANA, so rank 5 spends 60.0.",
  "one_home": "The cached cost lookup had one implementation, inside _stamp_resource_cost. Rather than a second copy in the champion module it moves to slotlib.extract_resource_cost beside extract_cooldown and extract_cast_time, and the engine calls it. That move is behaviour-preserving by construction -- same rule, same indexing, same memo -- and every number this slice moves comes from the Syndra stamp."
 },
 "landed_against": {
  "golden": "scripts/golden_baseline.json",
  "coupled_golden": "scripts/golden_coupled_baseline.json",
  "coupled_exact": "scripts/golden_coupled_exact.json",
  "rule": "R-17/R-32/D-97 -- no baseline moves inside this commit"
 },
 "qualifying_population": {
  "enumerated_before_first_src_edit": true,
  "rule": "R-20's second half. The count is not readable off the pre-change tree by inspection: the charge's price is an absent key, so what moves is every mana leaf standing at or after the charge in a fight that holds one, and how many that is depends on where the scheduler placed it. The population is therefore enumerated from committed artifacts before the first src/ edit, and its membership bounds what may qualify.",
  "enumerated_from": [
   "scripts/golden_baseline.json -- champion_baselines/Syndra, the parsed-entry dump",
   "scripts/golden_coupled_baseline.json -- every coupled scenario whose cast_timeline holds a Q2 row",
   "scripts/golden_coupled_exact.json -- the same scenarios in the exact capture"
  ],
  "the_population": "In the pair jurisdiction: the two keys the Q2 entry gains. In the coupled jurisdiction, per scenario holding a Q2 row: that row's resource_cost, every resource_before and resource_after from the charge onwards, and the fight's resource_spent and resource_remaining -- 16 leaves each. Four scenarios hold a Q2 row (syndra_custom_order_60/120 and syndra_derived_order_60/120); the two 39-splinter scenarios are below the 40-splinter threshold and hold none.",
  "size": {
   "golden": 2,
   "coupled_golden": 64,
   "coupled_exact": 0
  },
  "why_coupled_exact_is_zero": "The exact capture holds only totals -- five string-valued damage leaves per scenario -- and no cast timeline and no resource leaf. A mana move can reach it only by omitting a cast for insufficient mana, and no scenario comes near that: the deepest fight ends on 1213.2 of 1760.0.",
  "occurrences_outside_the_population": 0,
  "the_two_shape_counters": "/metadata/fingerprint/leaves and /metadata/fingerprint/numeric_leaves in the pair snapshot follow the two added keys by construction. They are the population's own census rather than members of it, which is why they are declared under golden_shape_counters and not counted in the size above."
 },
